%description:

Tcp.tsRecentAfterAckCheck:rfc -- TS.Recent takes the TSval of a segment that acknowledges unsent data, and PAWS then drops the ACKs of the peer.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "false: TS.Recent takes the TSval of each acceptable segment before its ACK
is processed (RFC 7323 section 5.3, R3); true: not from a segment that acknowledges data that
was not sent, as Linux".

The classes: rfc (false, the default) and linux (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::updateTsRecent() (RFC 7323 section 5.3, R3) takes the TSval of an acceptable
segment before its ACK is processed; with true, not from a segment that acknowledges data that
was not sent. This test separates "rfc" from "linux".

Host under test: host1, which sends 100000 bytes. The tap changes the first ACK of host2 that
acknowledges more than 20000 bytes: its ACK number goes 1000000 beyond the data that host1
sent, and its TSval 100000 ahead, as a forged segment would carry them. When TS.Recent takes
that TSval, PAWS (RFC 7323 section 5.3, R1) drops each later segment of host2, whose TSval is
older. Observation: level 2, the retransmission timer of host1 expires (the signal numRtos): the
later ACKs of host2 do not reach the connection.

%# parameter: Tcp.tsRecentAfterAckCheck
%# class: rfc
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tsRecentAfterAckCheck
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpTsRecentAfterAckCheckRfc")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host2").filterPacket("tcp.ackNo > {isn} + 1 + 20000").nth(1)
                     .set("tcp.ackNo", "tcp.ackNo + 1000000")
                     .mutate([](Packet *frame) { addToTsval(frame, 100000); })
                     .describe("the first ACK of host2 above 20000 bytes: an ACK of unsent data, and a TSval 100000 ahead"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("numRtos").describe("a timeout of host1").within(3.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpTsRecentAfterAckCheckRfc compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tsRecentAfterAckCheck = false    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpTsRecentAfterAckCheckRfc: PASS
